description:
Found by an external review and re-measured by architect-bb193f43 at main 0c215e82 on 2026-09-11.

MEASURED, in `apps/daemon/src/orchestrator/node-lander.ts`:

    const delivered = [...deliveredPaths(before.entries, observed.observation.entries), ...earlier];
    if (delivered.length === 0) {
      return refuse(nodeRef, brief.workspace, verifierReceiptId, {
        code: "NOTHING_TO_COMMIT", detail: "no path in the workspace differs from the staffing baseline",
      });
    }
    ...
    const checked = await checkLandingVerification({ ... });

`checkLandingVerification` is the only thing that compares the delivered workspace with the tree the verifier actually accepted, and the early return sits ABOVE it. So the one path that claims "nothing changed" is precisely the path that never checks whether the workspace still matches what was verified.

THE REPRODUCTION the review ran: verify changed code, restore the original bytes before landing, and the lander answers an outcome that is then treated as "no effect" - without ever detecting the mismatch.

WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT. This is a LANDING-EVIDENCE defect. It is NOT proof of a complete release bypass: criterion verification is a separate safeguard and still runs. Do not widen the row's claims beyond what the reproduction shows.

RELATED, AND NOT A DUPLICATE. task-f7d38f752b (DONE 2026-09-10) made a no-effect landing COUNT toward goal progress via `landedWithNoEffect`, deliberately crediting a NOTHING_TO_COMMIT receipt whose acceptance journaled no intent. That rule assumes the no-effect answer is TRUE. This row makes the lander establish that it is true before answering. Read that row's completionSummary in get_context.epicSiblings before planning - its `journaledIntents` reasoning is the context for why the early return matters more now, not less.

VERIFY BEFORE PLANNING with `grep -n 'NOTHING_TO_COMMIT' apps/daemon/src/orchestrator/node-lander.ts` and read the surrounding function; do not plan against the excerpt above.
